# Host branches (`wasmmod` vs `master`)

`wasmmod` = clean upy-shaped integration + `extmod/wasmmod` submodule (upstream PR track).
`master` = Metal product tree; **must keep `wasmmod` as a git ancestor**.

Canonical write-up: [`BRANCHES.md`](../../BRANCHES.md) (this package repo root).

## Invariant

```sh
git merge-base --is-ancestor origin/wasmmod origin/master && echo OK
```

If that fails, merge (or rebase) `wasmmod` into `master` before more product work.

## Submodule bumps

1. Land changes in `pymergetic/wasmmod` `main` first.
2. Bump `extmod/wasmmod` on metalpython **`wasmmod`** (µPy commit style + `Signed-off-by` last — feeds upstream PR CI).
3. Fast-forward / merge **`master`** onto that tip; do **not** dual-commit the same bump on both branches in parallel.

`wasmmod` (package repo default branch) ≠ metalpython host branch `wasmmod`.
